        <briefdescription>
<para>Decodes a Node object into an AnimationSpecification object. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function takes in a const reference to a Node object and a reference to an <ref refid="struct_a_g_e_1_1_animation_specification" kindref="compound">AGE::AnimationSpecification</ref> object. It checks if the Node is a sequence and if it has any elements. If these conditions are not met, it returns false. Otherwise, it populates the AnimationSpecification with data from the Node. The function then returns true.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>node</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The const reference to the Node object to be decoded. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The reference to the <ref refid="struct_a_g_e_1_1_animation_specification" kindref="compound">AGE::AnimationSpecification</ref> object that will hold the decoded data.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Returns true if the Node was successfully decoded, false otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
